// Runs workflows on the robots of a stack. A workflow (workflow/v1) says what
// the robots do, a run (run/v1) binds its roles to robots, and a workflow
// bundle (workflow_bundle/v1) carries a workflow with the digest of each of
// its files and the lock of the versions it ran with. The library
// workflow_documents of public-peppy-libs defines these documents and the
// JSON texts of the results here. A document, the roles of a run and
// caller_data cross as JSON5 text, and a bundle as the files of its
// directory, each path relative to it, so `peppy node call
// workflow_director_inst run --file bundle=@<dir>` sends one.
//
// The director checks a workflow against the contracts of the fleet listing.
// A run reads a fresh fleet listing, refuses a halted stack, binds each role
// to a robot of the listing, checks the workflow against the contracts of
// those robots, compares the lock of a bundle, takes the leases of the bound
// robots, each under the name `run <id>` of its run, lists the locations of
// the skills of each role and refuses a run that names a location a skill of
// its role does not know (locations:v1, which the director calls whatever the
// allowed contracts), checks the assumptions, then runs the initialization of
// each role and its lane. A run calls only the members of the allowed
// contracts of the director. No member here has the mark `moves_robot`: the
// director asks the daemon (robot_leases.check_move) before each call of a
// member with that mark, under its own leases. A read of an observation ends
// with the bound of the step that reads it. A read of a topic before its
// first message waits for it, up to the max_age_s of the observation past
// the start of the run, and is stale after. A check outside a step (an
// assumption, each check of a resume, success and minimum) has a bound of
// 30 s on the run clock, and a read in it that leader_streaming refuses goes
// again every second.
//
// A caller that offers leases to the director (robot_leases.offer) before it
// calls run lends them to that run: the run takes the leases of the robots
// it binds, and gives each back, closed, before it ends. A run binds a robot
// with no robot commander of its own, and never a robot that another run of
// the director binds.
//
// run, resume and abort report progress at each event of the run and at
// least every 5 s of wall time. The first progress of run is run_starts,
// which names the run (`r<N>`) and gives its run/v1 document. A cancel of run
// or resume, and the loss of its sender, aborts the run. The goal completes
// only for a completed run, with the run result; it ends cancelled for an
// aborted run, with the run and its result; and it fails for each other end
// with the kind that names it, its last progress giving the run result or,
// for a suspended run, the suspension. A suspended run has no running goal
// and waits for resume or abort. run_events gives the events of every run,
// and the end of a run (run_ends) only after the director released each
// lease of the run. A request that does not parse, or that gives both a
// run_document and roles, or neither or both of a workflow and a bundle, is
// refused with rejected and starts no run; every other run starts, and a
// check that refuses it ends it with run_refused.
//
// The fields of an event are empty where they do not apply: step names
// `<role>.<id>` (an item of a for_each adds `#<index>`), failure_kind is the
// kind of a failed step, an incident, a failed lane and the end of the run,
// and details is JSON of the types of workflow_documents: the run document
// at run_starts, the assumptions to confirm at to_confirm, the differences
// from the lock at differences, the named result at step_ends, the incident
// record at incident, the lane state at lane_suspends, lane_resumes and
// lane_ends, the suspension at run_suspends, the run result at run_ends, and
// the state of the run at progress.
//
// A failed step gives a failure kind: a kind of peppy, a kind of the
// contract of its call, or a kind that only the director gives:
// condition_failed (a fail_when is true), bound_reached (a loop hit its
// bound first), invariant_violated (an invariant is false), breaker_open (a
// repeat_until reached the max_failures of its breaker), stale_observation
// (a topic read is older than its max_age_s, or the topic has given no
// message in its max_age_s since the run started), stopped (another client
// stopped the goal), anomaly (the anomaly monitor gives an anomaly), alert
// (a bound physical robot raised an alert:v1 alert of severity 2 or 3, or an
// alert set of its nodes went stale), signal_unreachable (every lane that can
// emit a signal that a wait_for awaits has ended) and clock_stopped (the
// simulation clock stood still for 10 s of wall time while a lane ran).
//
// The anomaly monitor of a run is a service of an allowed contract whose
// request is { robot: string, step: string } and whose response is
// { anomaly: bool, kind: string, severity: low | medium | high, description:
// string, frame: bytes }. A member that names a run the director does not
// know gets an error reply, or a refusal, with rejected; one that the state
// of the run does not admit, with precondition_failed.
//
// The mcp_exposure/v1 document workflow_controls:v1 of mcp-hub selects
// every member but replay, which reads a journal for a program, locations,
// which teaches the skills of a robot, and the topic run_events, whose
// events the progress of run, resume and abort gives.
{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "workflow_director",
    tag: "v1",
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    run_degraded: "The run ended degraded: its lanes ended, success is false and minimum is true",
    run_failed: "The run ended failed",
    run_refused: "The run was refused before its initialization; the message names the cause",
    run_halted: "A halt ended the run",
    run_interrupted: "The leases of the run ended, or a move check refused a call, with no halt, or the director stopped during the run",
    run_suspended: "The run is suspended, or a resume was refused and it stays suspended; the message names the cause",
  },
  interfaces: {
    services: [
      {
        // The fleet listing within the allowed contracts: each robot with
        // only its allowed contracts, and the pinned document of each of
        // those contracts. Refused with resource_unavailable before the
        // director has read the fleet listing.
        name: "robots",
        response_message_format: {
          halted: "bool",
          robots: {
            $type: "array",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              name: "string",
              kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["simulated", "physical"] },
              // The model that robot_identity:v1 of the robot reports; empty
              // until it answers, or without robot_identity:v1.
              model: "string",
              // The robot commander of the robot; empty when it has none.
              robot_commander: "string",
              software: { $type: "string", $enum: ["running", "stopped"] },
              // The holder and the name of the lease of the robot, and
              // whether it is open; empty and false with no lease.
              lease_holder: "string",
              lease_name: "string",
              lease_open: "bool",
              contracts: {
                $type: "array",
                $items: {
                  $type: "object",
                  name: "string",
                  tag: "string",
                  sha256: "string",
                  // The name in the robot of each instance that implements
                  // the contract.
                  instances: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
                },
              },
            },
          },
          documents: {
            $type: "array",
            $items: { $type: "object", name: "string", tag: "string", sha256: "string", document: "string" },
          },
        },
      },
      {
        // Checks a workflow by every rule of the checker. Without roles, the
        // check reads each pinned document of each of its contracts in the
        // fleet listing. With roles, a JSON5 object from each role to a
        // robot name of the listing, it also checks the binding. Each error
        // names its step as `<role>.<id>` or its field by its path; a
        // workflow that does not parse gives one error with an empty `at`.
        // Refused with rejected for roles that do not parse or that name
        // "auto", and before the first fleet listing with
        // resource_unavailable, as robots is.
        name: "check",
        request_message_format: {
          workflow: "string",
          roles: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
        },
        response_message_format: {
          passed: "bool",
          errors: { $type: "array", $items: { $type: "object", at: "string", message: "string" } },
        },
      },
      {
        // Confirms an assumption without a check of a run that waits for
        // its confirmations. Refused with rejected for an assumption the
        // run does not have, and with precondition_failed for one with a
        // check, one confirmed already, or a run that does not wait for
        // confirmations.
        name: "confirm",
        request_message_format: { run: "string", assumption: "string" },
      },
      {
        // Asks a running run to suspend: the director cancels each running
        // goal of the run and runs the safe_state of each running lane. The
        // progress of the run reports each suspension. Refused with
        // precondition_failed for a run that does not run.
        name: "suspend",
        request_message_format: { run: "string" },
      },
      {
        // The runs that the director keeps, newest first, those of earlier
        // processes of the director included.
        name: "runs",
        response_message_format: {
          runs: {
            $type: "array",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              run: "string",
              workflow: "string",
              revision: "u32",
              state: {
                $type: "string",
                $enum: ["preparing", "confirming", "running", "suspended", "ending", "completed", "degraded", "failed", "refused", "aborted", "halted", "interrupted"],
              },
              started_by: "string",
              robots: {
                $type: "array",
                $items: { $type: "object", role: "string", robot: "string", leased: "bool", open: "bool" },
              },
            },
          },
        },
      },
      {
        // The state of one run, and its details as JSON: the run status of
        // workflow_documents, with the run result of an ended run.
        name: "status",
        request_message_format: { run: "string" },
        response_message_format: {
          state: {
            $type: "string",
            $enum: ["preparing", "confirming", "running", "suspended", "ending", "completed", "degraded", "failed", "refused", "aborted", "halted", "interrupted"],
          },
          details: "string",
        },
      },
      {
        // The journal of one run, as JSON Lines.
        name: "journal",
        request_message_format: { run: "string" },
        response_message_format: { journal: "string" },
      },
      {
        // Replays a journal with no robot, by the run that wrote it or as
        // its text, and compares each decision with the journal: `same`
        // when each matches, else `difference` gives the first that does
        // not, as JSON of what the journal holds and what the replay gives.
        name: "replay",
        request_message_format: {
          run: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
          journal: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
        },
        response_message_format: { same: "bool", decisions: "u32", difference: "string" },
      },
    ],
    actions: [
      {
        // Teaches or lists the locations of the skills of `robot`: each
        // instance of the robot that implements locations:v1, as the fleet
        // listing names them. With teach, the director teaches each of them
        // the locations given, each as teach of locations:v1 takes it, and
        // gives the locations each knows after; without, it gives the
        // locations each knows. A teach on a robot with a lease is refused
        // with precondition_failed, naming the holder and the name of the
        // lease, so no teach changes the locations of a robot of a run or of
        // an apply; a teach holds the robot while it runs, under a lease
        // named `locations`, and no run of the director binds the robot until
        // the teach ends. Refused with rejected for a robot the listing does
        // not hold, with resource_unavailable before the first fleet listing
        // and for a robot with no instance of locations:v1, and with the kind
        // of a refusal of a skill, naming the instance.
        name: "locations",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            robot: "string",
            teach: {
              $type: "array",
              $optional: true,
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                name: "string",
                kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["pose", "landmark", "surface", "region"] },
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
                size: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
              },
            },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            // One entry per instance of the robot that implements
            // locations:v1, each with the locations it knows.
            skills: {
              $type: "array",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                instance: "string",
                locations: {
                  $type: "array",
                  $items: {
                    $type: "object",
                    name: "string",
                    kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["pose", "landmark", "surface", "region"] },
                    position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
                    orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
                    size: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
                  },
                },
              },
            },
          },
        },
      },
      {
        // Runs a workflow, given as workflow or in a bundle, by a run/v1
        // document or by roles (a JSON5 object from roles to robot names;
        // each role it leaves out takes "auto", and the run is attended),
        // until the run ends or suspends. started_by labels the run in the
        // list of runs, and the journal and the run result keep
        // caller_data, JSON5 text that the director reads no field of.
        name: "run",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            workflow: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
            bundle: {
              $type: "array",
              $optional: true,
              $items: { $type: "object", path: "string", content: "string" },
            },
            run_document: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
            roles: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
            started_by: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
            caller_data: { $type: "string", $optional: true },
          },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            run: "string",
            role: "string",
            event: {
              $type: "string",
              $enum: ["run_starts", "to_confirm", "differences", "initialization_starts", "actions_start", "step_starts", "step_ends", "lane_suspends", "lane_resumes", "lane_ends", "incident", "run_suspends", "run_ends", "progress"],
            },
            step: "string",
            failure_kind: "string",
            message: "string",
            details: "string",
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: { run: "string", result: "string" },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["run_degraded", "run_failed", "run_refused", "run_halted", "run_interrupted", "run_suspended"],
      },
      {
        // Resumes a suspended run: it closes the open lease of each robot of
        // the suspended lanes, checks the done_when of each cancelled or
        // failed call, the invariant of each enclosing step and the reach
        // checks of the roles, then goes on until the run ends or suspends.
        // A refused resume fails with run_suspended after a run_suspends
        // event whose suspension names the false check, and opens those
        // leases again.
        name: "resume",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: { run: "string" },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            run: "string",
            role: "string",
            event: {
              $type: "string",
              $enum: ["run_starts", "to_confirm", "differences", "initialization_starts", "actions_start", "step_starts", "step_ends", "lane_suspends", "lane_resumes", "lane_ends", "incident", "run_suspends", "run_ends", "progress"],
            },
            step: "string",
            failure_kind: "string",
            message: "string",
            details: "string",
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: { run: "string", result: "string" },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["run_degraded", "run_failed", "run_refused", "run_halted", "run_interrupted", "run_suspended"],
      },
      {
        // Aborts a run: it closes each open lease of the run, cancels each
        // running goal, runs the safe_state of each running lane and no
        // safe_state of a suspended lane, and completes once the run ended
        // aborted and its leases are released, with the run result. For a
        // run that has ended, it completes at once with its result.
        name: "abort",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: { run: "string" },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            run: "string",
            role: "string",
            event: {
              $type: "string",
              $enum: ["run_starts", "to_confirm", "differences", "initialization_starts", "actions_start", "step_starts", "step_ends", "lane_suspends", "lane_resumes", "lane_ends", "incident", "run_suspends", "run_ends", "progress"],
            },
            step: "string",
            failure_kind: "string",
            message: "string",
            details: "string",
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: { run: "string", result: "string" },
        },
      },
    ],
    topics: [
      {
        // Every event of every run, as the progress of run, resume and abort
        // gives the events of its run.
        name: "run_events",
        qos_profile: "reliable",
        message_format: {
          run: "string",
          role: "string",
          event: {
            $type: "string",
            $enum: ["run_starts", "to_confirm", "differences", "initialization_starts", "actions_start", "step_starts", "step_ends", "lane_suspends", "lane_resumes", "lane_ends", "incident", "run_suspends", "run_ends"],
          },
          step: "string",
          failure_kind: "string",
          message: "string",
          details: "string",
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
